I have gathered a thorough picture. Here is my report.

## Repository overview

This is the OfficeFloor/Spring Boot version of `spring-petclinic-rest`. Build system is **Maven** (`/home/daniel/sandbox/pom.xml`, with `mvnw` wrapper). The create-owner request is processed by a chain of small "function" classes wired together in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`. Response DTOs (`OwnerDto`, `OwnerFieldsDto`, `OwnerPageDto`) are **generated at build time** by the `openapi-generator-maven-plugin` from `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` into package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto` (there are no hand-written DTO files under `src`).

---

## 1. Membership identifier (membershipNumber)

File: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignMembershipNumber.java`

```java
public class AssignMembershipNumber {

    public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
        int yy = owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100;
        owner.setMembershipNumber(String.format("%s-M%02d", owner.getCustomerCode(), yy));
    }
}
```

Format is `<customerCode>-M<YY>` where YY = last two digits of the (business-day-adjusted) `registrationDate` year. This is the year segment you referenced. The field is stored on the model (`Owner.membershipNumber`, getter/setter at `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` lines 69-70, 177-183) and documented in the OpenAPI schema at `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` lines 2134-2139.

---

## 2. Tenure (365-day windows from registration date)

File: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignMembershipLevel.java`

```java
public class AssignMembershipLevel {

    /** Tenure, in days, above which the owner qualifies for the tenure points. */
    private static final long TENURE_THRESHOLD_DAYS = 365;

    /** Household size at or above which the household points are awarded. */
    private static final int HOUSEHOLD_THRESHOLD = 3;

    public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
        int points = 0;
        if (owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank()) {
            points += 2;
        }
        if (owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0) {
            points += 1;
        }
        if (owner.getHouseholdSize() != null && owner.getHouseholdSize() >= HOUSEHOLD_THRESHOLD) {
            points += 2;
        }
        if (tenureDays(owner) > TENURE_THRESHOLD_DAYS) {
            points += 3;
        }
        owner.setMembershipPoints(points);
        owner.setMembershipLevel(levelForPoints(points));
    }

    private static int levelForPoints(int points) {
        if (points <= 1) {
            return 1;
        }
        if (points <= 3) {
            return 2;
        }
        if (points <= 5) {
            return 3;
        }
        return 4;
    }

    private static long tenureDays(Owner owner) {
        LocalDate registrationDate = owner.getRegistrationDate();
        if (registrationDate == null) {
            return 0;
        }
        return ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now());
    }
}
```

`tenureDays()` is the tenure computation (days between registrationDate and today); the `> 365` check is the "365-day window" logic. Note tenure is not itself exposed as a field — it only feeds `membershipPoints`/`membershipLevel` (OpenAPI schema lines 2169-2185).

---

## 3. Business-day-adjusted registration date

File: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BusinessDay.java`

```java
final class BusinessDay {

    /** Fixed public-holiday calendar; a date landing on any of these rolls forward. */
    private static final Set<LocalDate> HOLIDAYS = Set.of(
            LocalDate.of(2026, 1, 1),
            LocalDate.of(2026, 1, 26),
            LocalDate.of(2026, 4, 25),
            LocalDate.of(2026, 12, 25),
            LocalDate.of(2026, 12, 28));

    private BusinessDay() {
    }

    static LocalDate adjust(LocalDate date) {
        while (date.getDayOfWeek() == DayOfWeek.SATURDAY || date.getDayOfWeek() == DayOfWeek.SUNDAY
                || HOLIDAYS.contains(date)) {
            date = date.plusDays(1);
        }
        return date;
    }
}
```

This is package-private (`final class BusinessDay`, no `public`). It is applied to the registration date in `BuildOwner` and re-computed in `RejectOverDailyLimit`:

File: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java`

```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerMapper ownerMapper, Out<Owner> built) {
    Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(request);
    LocalDate effective = owner.getRegistrationDate() != null ? owner.getRegistrationDate() : LocalDate.now();
    owner.setRegistrationDate(BusinessDay.adjust(effective));
    built.set(owner);
}
```

File: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RejectOverDailyLimit.java` (lines 25-26) also calls `BusinessDay.adjust(effective)` to count owners on the adjusted day. So every date-derived value (membership-number year, daily limit) uses the adjusted date. This is the key place a fiscal-year change would need to hook in.

---

## 4. fiscalYear

There is currently **no `fiscalYear` field, function, or schema entry in `src/main`.** `grep -rniE "fiscal" src/main` returns nothing; `openapi.yml` has no fiscal entry. The only reference is in the test (below), which asserts a `fiscalYear` field that does not yet exist — this is the feature to be implemented. Per the test's Javadoc: "Move date-derived values to a fiscal-year basis, where the fiscal year starts on 1 July." A `fiscalYear` returned as `FY\d{2}`.

To add it you would: add a `fiscalYear` property to the `OwnerDto` schema in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` (alongside the other readOnly derived fields around lines 2128-2198), and add a MapStruct `@Mapping(target = "fiscalYear", expression = ...)` in the mapper (pattern shown below). The membership-number YY and tenure logic would then also move to the fiscal-year basis.

---

## 5. Response DTO / mapping of these values

The DTO is generated, but the derived values are wired via MapStruct in:

File: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`

```java
@Mapper(uses = PetMapper.class)
public interface OwnerMapper {

    @Mapping(target = "displayName",
            expression = "java(owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName())")
    @Mapping(target = "initials",
            expression = "java(owner.getFirstName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \".\" + owner.getLastName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \".\")")
    @Mapping(target = "checkDigit", expression = "java(...CheckDigit.of(owner.getCustomerCode()))")
    @Mapping(target = "householdId", expression = "java(...HouseholdId.of(owner.getLastName(), owner.getPostcode()))")
    @Mapping(target = "identityKey", expression = "java(...IdentityKey.of(...))")
    @Mapping(target = "locality", expression = "java(...Locality.ofCustomerCode(owner.getCustomerCode()))")
    @Mapping(target = "timezone", expression = "java(...Timezone.of(...))")
    @Mapping(target = "contactPreference", expression = "java(...)")
    @Mapping(target = "ageBand", expression = "java(...AgeBand.of(owner))")
    @Mapping(target = "telephoneDisplay", expression = "java(...TelephoneDisplay.of(owner.getTelephone()))")
    @Mapping(target = "salutation", expression = "java(...)")
    OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);
    ...
}
```

`membershipNumber`, `membershipLevel`, `membershipPoints`, `registrationDate` are mapped by name automatically (they exist on both `Owner` and `OwnerDto`). Derived-only fields (like a future `fiscalYear`) follow the `@Mapping(target=..., expression=...)` pattern above. This mapper is the single funnel through which every read response (`RespondWithOwner`, `RespondWithOwnerCreated`, `RespondWithOwnerUpdated`, list endpoints) builds its DTO.

Response function classes (all in `.../rest/function/owner/`):
- `RespondWithOwnerCreated.java` — 201 for POST /api/owners (calls `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto`)
- `RespondWithOwner.java` — GET /api/owners/{id}
- `RespondWithOwnerUpdated.java` — PUT

Audit log of these values: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java` logs `registrationDate`, `membershipLevel`, `membershipNumber`.

---

## Tests

Only the acceptance tests touch these concepts. Test package: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/`

File: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` (the active/current test — expects the not-yet-implemented fiscalYear):

```java
/** fiscal-year: Move date-derived values to a fiscal-year basis, where the fiscal year starts on 1 July. R... */
class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {

    @Test
    void coreReturnsFiscalYear() throws Exception {
        int id = createOwnerOk(structuredOwner());
        JsonNode n = fetchOwner(id);
        assertTrue(n.get("fiscalYear").asText().matches("FY\\d{2}"));
    }
}
```

File: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — base class with helpers (`createOwnerOk`, `structuredOwner`, `fetchOwner`, `ownerNode`) and, importantly, a mirror of the business-day roll used to compute expected dates (lines 239-274):

```java
/** Fixed public holidays the business-day roll skips (year of the run). */
protected static final Set<LocalDate> HOLIDAYS = Set.of(
        LocalDate.parse("2026-01-01"), LocalDate.parse("2026-01-26"),
        LocalDate.parse("2026-04-25"), LocalDate.parse("2026-12-25"), LocalDate.parse("2026-12-28"));

/** Roll a date forward over weekends and pinned holidays to the next business day. */
protected LocalDate toBusinessDay(LocalDate d) {
    while (d.getDayOfWeek() == DayOfWeek.SATURDAY || d.getDayOfWeek() == DayOfWeek.SUNDAY
            || HOLIDAYS.contains(d)) {
        d = d.plusDays(1);
    }
    return d;
}
```

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java` is a test support class (captures the audit log). There are no dedicated unit tests for `AssignMembershipNumber`, `AssignMembershipLevel`, or `BusinessDay`; coverage is only through the acceptance layer.

---

## Build system and running tests

- Maven, via the wrapper `/home/daniel/sandbox/mvnw`. Java/Spring Boot project; DTOs generated during the `generate-sources` phase by `openapi-generator-maven-plugin` (pom.xml lines 370-388, `inputSpec=src/main/resources/openapi.yml`, `modelPackage=org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto`). Because DTOs are generated, adding `fiscalYear` requires editing `openapi.yml` and rebuilding.
- Run the full test suite: `./mvnw test` (from `/home/daniel/sandbox`).
- Run just the acceptance test: `./mvnw test -Dtest=AcceptanceTest`.
- Full verify (includes any integration/failsafe): `./mvnw verify`.

Note: I did not find explicit surefire/failsafe or custom test-run instructions in `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` beyond standard Maven usage; `spring-boot-starter-test` and `woof_test` are the test dependencies (pom.xml lines 140, 160).

